269
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:23,080
attending within 6 months of signing up,

270
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:26,040
and of the people who join specifically

271
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:27,600
as a January resolution, up to 80% have

272
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:29,440
quit showing up by the time summer

273
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:31,440
arrives. February tends to be the

274
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:33,040
highest risk month of all, the point

275
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:35,400
where the initial burst of motivation

276
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:37,360
fades before a real habit is formed.

277
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:39,480
Experienced owners don't panic about

278
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:41,680
this. They plan their entire cash flow

279
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:43,080
around it using the January surge to

280
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:44,760
build a reserve that carries them

281
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:47,120
through the quieter summer months when

282
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:48,560
new sign-ups slow down. The owners who

283
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:50,920
get caught off guard are the ones who

284
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:52,760
spend that January windfall as if it

285
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:54,800
were a permanent ongoing level of

286
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:56,640
revenue instead of the seasonal spike

287
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:58,400
that it actually is. There's also a

288
00:09:56,640 --> 00:10:00,360
structural choice that sits underneath

289
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:02,360
all of this. Whether to build an

290
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:04,440
independent gym from the ground up or

291
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:06,240
buy into an established franchise. A

292
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:08,280
franchise gives you an already known

293
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:10,400
brand name, a proven layout,

294
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:12,080
standardized software, and often better

295
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:14,200
pricing on equipment through corporate

296
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:16,440
purchasing deals. That's valuable,

297
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:18,440
especially for a first-time owner, but

298
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:20,320
it isn't free. Franchise agreements

299
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:23,920
typically require an upfront franchise

300
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:26,520
fee of 20 to $60,000, an ongoing royalty

301
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:28,400
of 5 to 10% of gross revenue paid back

302
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:30,600
to the parent company every month, and

303
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:32,480
an additional contribution of around 2%

304
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:34,680
of revenue into a shared national

305
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:36,320
marketing fund. An independent owner

306
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:38,720
keeps every dollar of profit the

307
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:40,560
business generates. A franchise owner is

308
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:42,120
permanently sharing a slice of the top

309
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:44,040
line in exchange for the brand

310
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:46,120
recognition and support system, which

311
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:47,400
can be worth it, but only if the extra

312
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:49,680
membership volume that brand name

313
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:52,360
attracts is large enough to cover what

314
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:54,360
you're handing back every month. Now,

315
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:56,080
here's where the psychology becomes just

316
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:57,720
as important as the math.

317
00:10:56,080 --> 00:11:00,040
Why do people keep paying for something

318
00:10:57,720 --> 00:11:01,800
they don't use? Part of it is optimism

319
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:03,480
at the moment of signing up. The

320
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:05,600
membership feels like a promise to a

321
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:07,240
future version of yourself. Part of it

322
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:09,200
is what economists call a commitment

323
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:11,240
device. Paying for the gym is meant to

324
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:13,360
be the thing that forces you to go. And

325
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:15,640
part of it is pure inertia. Canceling

326
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:18,480
requires admitting the plan didn't work,

327
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:20,160
and for a monthly fee of 10 to $30, most

328
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:22,280
people would rather quietly keep paying

329
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:24,360
than confront that. The physical design

330
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:26,920
of the gym reinforces this, whether

331
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:28,640
members notice it or not. Clean, simple

332
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:30,920
layouts with clear pathways reduce the

333
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:32,840
sense of intimidation a new member feels

334
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:34,520
walking in for the first time, which

335
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:36,440
keeps them coming back long enough for

336
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:38,680
the habit to either form or quietly

337
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:40,280
fade. Mirrors placed around the strength

338
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:42,880
area help people track their own

339
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:44,120
progress, which can boost motivation,

340
00:11:42,880 --> 00:11:46,360
but too many mirrors in a

341
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:48,440
beginner-friendly zone can backfire and

342
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:50,480
increase self-consciousness instead.

343
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:52,480
Lighting is chosen deliberately, too.

344
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:54,360
Weight rooms are often lit with harder,

345
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:56,200
more directional light that creates

346
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:58,320
visible muscle definition, while

347
00:11:56,200 --> 00:12:00,600
stretching and recovery areas use softer

348
00:11:58,320 --> 00:12:02,720
lighting to feel calmer. Even the music

349
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:04,280
tempo is chosen with a purpose. Since

350
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:06,080
faster music has been shown to help

351
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:07,880
people push through a workout with less

352
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:10,000
perceived effort. None of this is

353
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:11,880
decoration. It's all aimed at the same

354
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,320
target, keeping a member emotionally

355
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:15,160
attached to the gym for as long as

356
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:18,120
possible, whether or not they're using

357
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:20,000
it every week. And gyms know this, which

358
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:22,000
is why the process of leaving a gym is

359
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:24,120
almost never as easy as the process of

360
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:26,240
joining one. Many membership contracts

361
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:28,440
require you to cancel in writing, not by

362
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:30,480
phone, not through an app, but in person

363
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:32,600
at the club or through certified mail

364
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:34,880
with a return receipt. Contracts often

365
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:36,880
require 30 to 60 days of advance notice

366
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:38,720
before the next billing cycle, which

367
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:40,480
guarantees the gym collects at least one

368
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:42,520
more month of dues even after you've

369
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:45,160
decided to leave. And when a credit card

370
00:12:42,520 --> 00:12:47,600
expires or a payment fails, that alone

371
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:49,839
accounts for roughly 30 to 40% of all

372
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:51,880
cancellations, which is why gyms run

373
00:12:49,839 --> 00:12:53,880
entire departments dedicated to chasing

374
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:56,280
down failed payments before a member can

375
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:58,360
drift away entirely. This friction has

376
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:59,680
not gone unnoticed by regulators. The

377
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:02,280
Federal Trade Commission tried to

378
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:04,200
introduce a national rule in 2024

379
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:07,480
requiring that canceling a subscription

380
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:09,400
be just as easy as signing up for one.

381
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:11,240
A federal appeals court struck that rule

382
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:13,600
down on procedural grounds in the summer

383
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:15,800
of 2025, and the agency has since

384
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:17,720
restarted the process. Some cities have

385
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:19,280
moved on their own. New York City, for

386
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:21,120
example, introduced a local

387
00:13:19,280 --> 00:13:24,080
click-to-cancel rule that took effect in

388
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:27,040
October of 2026, with penalties of over

389
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:29,400
$500 per violation for gyms that make

390
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:31,040
canceling deliberately difficult.

391
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:32,520
Keep this in mind because it tells you

392
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:34,040
something important about the business

393
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:36,120
you're considering.

394
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:38,680
If a gym's survival depended on happy,

395
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:40,280
engaged, frequently attending members,

396
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:42,320
it wouldn't need to make canceling this

397
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:44,160
hard. The fact that cancellation

398
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:46,120
friction is such a core part of gym

399
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:47,840
operations tells you the business

400
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:49,840
already knows a large share of its

401
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:51,680
revenue comes from people who wish they

402
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:53,640
weren't paying. Before we get to what

403
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:55,720
can go wrong, there's a second layer of

404
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:57,720
hidden cost that catches almost every

405
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:59,640
first-time gym owner off guard and it

406
00:13:57,720 --> 00:14:01,920
has nothing to do with treadmills. It's

407
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:04,160
the music. Playing background music in a

408
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:05,880
commercial space is not the same as

409
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:07,880
playing it in your living room. In the

410
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:09,840
United States, any business playing

411
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:11,760
music for its customers is legally

412
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:13,640
required to pay for a public performance

413
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:15,920
license and there isn't just one

414
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:18,120
organization to pay. There are several

415
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:19,920
performing rights organizations, each

416
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:21,120
representing different songwriters and

417
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:23,040
publishers,

418
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:24,440
and a gym typically needs to be licensed

419
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:27,000
with more than one of them at the same

420
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:29,200
time. The minimum annual fees for each

421
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:32,320
of these licenses can run anywhere from

422
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:34,040
around 200 to close to $600. And once

423
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:36,040
you're paying all of them together, the

424
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:39,040
combined bill for a single location can

425
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:40,960
land somewhere between $1,300 and $4,000

426
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:43,600
a year. Skip this and the risk isn't a

427
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:45,680
small one. These licensing organizations

428
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:48,160
send field investigators into gyms,

429
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:50,360
bars, and retail spaces specifically to

430
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:52,680
check for unlicensed music. Under

431
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:54,440
federal copyright law, statutory damages

432
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:58,360
for willful infringement can run from

433
00:14:54,440 --> 00:15:01,440
$750 per song all the way up $30,000 per

434
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:03,360
song and as high as $150,000

435
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:05,360
per song if a court decides the

436
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:07,320
infringement was intentional. A gym

437
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:08,880
owner who assumes a personal streaming

438
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:11,000
subscription is good enough for the

439
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:13,040
sound system has quietly taken on a

440
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,960
legal risk worth far more than the

441
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:16,920
license fee would have ever cost. That's

442
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:19,240
a small example, but it points at the

443
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:20,839
bigger lesson of this entire business.

444
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:23,160
Almost none of the real costs are the

445
00:15:20,839 --> 00:15:24,880
ones printed on the equipment catalog.

446
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:26,880
They're the ones buried in a licensing

447
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:29,000
agreement, a lease clause, or a

448
00:15:26,880 --> 00:15:31,080
maintenance contract that nobody reads

449
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:33,200
carefully until something breaks. And

450
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:35,280
plenty of things do break. Heavy daily

451
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:37,320
use wears down treadmill belts, strength

452
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:39,480
machine cables, and upholstery far

453
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:41,400
faster than home use ever would. And

454
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:44,600
mid-size gyms typically budget somewhere

455
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:46,280
between $1,000 and $3,000 a month just

456
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:48,600
for ongoing equipment repair and

457
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:50,520
replacement. Utility bills for a gym

458
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:52,760
running constant ventilation, bright

459
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:55,800
lighting, hot water for showers can run

460
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:57,320
between $1,000 and $6,000 a month. None

461
00:15:55,800 --> 00:16:00,080
of these numbers are dramatic on their

462
00:15:57,320 --> 00:16:02,160
own. Stack together, month after month,

463
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:03,800
they quietly eat into the exact margin

464
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:05,600
the owner was counting on. Now, let's

465
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:07,480
talk about whether a gym built entirely

466
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:09,360
on this quiet subscription model can

467
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:11,360
actually survive. Because the honest

468
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:13,040
answer is, sometimes not. Even at

469
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:15,720
enormous scale, meet Bally Total

470
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:17,600
Fitness. At its peak, it was the largest

471
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:19,600
health club chain in the United States

472
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:21,240
with locations across the country and a

473
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:23,400
business model built on aggressive

474
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:25,440
long-term membership contracts, often

475
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:27,600
financed over several years like a car

476
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:29,800
loan. On paper, the model looked

477
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:31,960
brilliant. Lock members into years of

478
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:33,920
guaranteed payments and you've secured

479
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:35,720
your revenue in advance. But, how does

480
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:37,640
the largest fitness chain in the country

481
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:39,920
end up filing for bankruptcy not once

482
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:41,839
but twice within the span of a single

483
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:43,920
year? The answer isn't that people

484
00:16:41,839 --> 00:16:45,920
stopped wanting to work out. The answer

485
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:47,680
is structural. The aggressive sales

486
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:49,839
tactics and long-term financing

487
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:52,200
contracts triggered consumer protection

488
00:16:49,839 --> 00:16:54,240
lawsuits and accounting investigations.

489
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:55,920
The company had built its empire on debt

490
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:58,160
and contractual promises rather than

491
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:59,760
genuine sustainable member value. And

492
00:16:58,160 --> 00:17:02,360
when the legal and financial pressure

493
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:05,280
mounted, the whole structure gave way.

494
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:07,920
Bally filed for bankruptcy in 2007 and

495
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:10,319
again in 2008 before its assets were

496
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:13,079
sold off piece by piece. A similar story

497
00:17:10,319 --> 00:17:14,600
played out with 24-Hour Fitness. Once

498
00:17:13,079 --> 00:17:16,280
one of the largest gym chains in the

499
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:18,640
country, it didn't collapse because

500
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:20,520
people stopped exercising. It collapsed

501
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:22,480
because it had taken on too much debt

502
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:25,319
relative to its actual cash flow. And

503
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:26,800
when that debt came due, scale alone

504
00:17:25,319 --> 00:17:28,880
wasn't enough to save it. Here's the

505
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:30,040
structural observation. Because that's

506
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:32,200
really the point of both of these

507
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:33,880
stories. Neither of these companies

508
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:35,600
failed because nobody wanted to buy a

509
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:38,120
gym membership. They failed because the

510
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:40,560
math connecting fixed costs, rent, debt

511
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:42,960
payments, equipment financing to actual

512
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:44,680
reliable revenue broke down. A gym with

513
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:46,960
thousands of members and full parking

514
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:48,840
lots can still be one bad debt structure

515
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:50,640
away from insolvency.

516
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:52,440
The visible crowd on the gym floor tells

517
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:54,600
you nothing about whether the underlying

518
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:56,760
financial structure can hold. So, how

519
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:58,640
does a gym actually make money in plain

520
00:17:56,760 --> 00:18:01,240
mechanical terms once it's passed all of

521
00:17:58,640 --> 00:18:02,920
this? The core engine is simple. Monthly

522
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:04,840
dues times number of members minus fixed

523
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:06,480
costs. If a gym has fixed monthly

524
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:08,080
operating costs, rent, payroll,

525
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:11,600
equipment payments, utilities,

526
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:14,160
insurance, software of around $30,000,

527
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:15,880
and it charges an average of $89 a month

528
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:18,840
per member, then it needs somewhere

529
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:21,040
around 337 paying members just to break

530
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:23,160
even. Below that number, the gym is

531
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:24,760
losing money every month. Above it,

532
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:27,120
additional members are almost pure

533
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:29,160
profit because remember, the marginal

534
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:31,320
cost of an inactive member is close to

535
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:33,320
zero. That's the good news. Here's the

536
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:34,920
volatility that comes right after it.

537
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:37,320
New gyms typically don't reach that

538
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:39,240
break even membership count on day one.

539
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:41,200
It can take 12 to 18 months of

540
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:43,480
accumulating members before the facility

541
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:45,160
crosses into profitability. And every

